@lang en
IMPORT `homecare-general-conditions`

-- Liberty HomeCare (UW-RPP-W-001-06-V): the General Exclusions (CÁC ĐIỀU KHOẢN LOẠI TRỪ
-- CHUNG), 1-9. They apply to every Part: "the Insurer shall not be liable for any loss,
-- destruction or damage, cost or expense, liability, bodily injury or accident ...".
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are line N of ../../source/raw/liberty-homecare.txt.
--
-- src:684 | CÁC ĐIỀU KHOẢN LOẠI TRỪ CHUNG
-- src:686 | Công Ty Bảo Hiểm sẽ không chịu trách nhiệm đối với:

§ `General Exclusions`

DECLARE `A General Exclusion` IS ONE OF
    `General Exclusion 1(a): war, invasion, hostilities or civil war`
    `General Exclusion 1(b): an act of terrorism`
    `General Exclusion 1(c): mutiny, rising, rebellion, usurped power, martial law or siege`
    `General Exclusion 1: action taken to control, prevent or suppress (a) to (c)`
    `General Exclusion 2: confiscation, requisition or destruction by order of an authority`
    `General Exclusion 3(a): nuclear weapons material`
    `General Exclusion 3(b)(i): ionising radiation or contamination from nuclear fuel or waste`
    `General Exclusion 3(b)(ii): a nuclear explosive assembly`
    `General Exclusion 4: asbestos`
    `General Exclusion 5: DES, dioxin, urea formaldehyde, SARS, AIDS, ARC or similar`
    `General Exclusion 6: wilful act or wilful negligence of the Insured`
    `General Exclusion 7(a): loss of or damage to Electronic Data`
    `General Exclusion 8: part of the Insured Location used to make, deposit or store goods`
    `General Exclusion 9: sanctions`

§§ `The exclusions`

-- 1. Any loss ... directly or indirectly caused by or connected with "any act of terrorism"
-- regardless of any other cause contributing concurrently or in any sequence:
-- (a) war, invasion, act of foreign enemy, hostilities or warlike operations (whether war be
-- declared or not), civil war; (b) acts of terrorism; (c) mutiny, rising of the military or
-- the people, insurrection, rebellion, military or usurped power, "luật hôn nhân" (literally
-- "marriage law", where martial law is meant; finding X-translation), state of siege, or any event
-- proclaiming or maintaining them; (d) an excluded risk.
