GIVEN circumstances IS A LIST OF `A circumstance of a loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A General Exclusion`
`General Exclusions 2 to 6 apply to` circumstances MEANS
    `those that hold among`
        (LIST PAIR `General Exclusion 2: confiscation, requisition or destruction by order of an authority`
                   (`it was` `confiscation, requisition or destruction by order of government or local authority`)
            , PAIR `General Exclusion 3(a): nuclear weapons material` (`it was` `nuclear weapons material`)
            , PAIR `General Exclusion 3(b)(i): ionising radiation or contamination from nuclear fuel or waste`
                   (`it was` `ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or waste`)
            , PAIR `General Exclusion 3(b)(ii): a nuclear explosive assembly`
                   (`it was` `radioactive, toxic, explosive or hazardous properties of a nuclear explosive assembly`)
            , PAIR `General Exclusion 4: asbestos` (`it was` `asbestos`)
            , PAIR `General Exclusion 5: DES, dioxin, urea formaldehyde, SARS, AIDS, ARC or similar`
                   (`it was` `DES, dioxin, urea formaldehyde, SARS, AIDS, ARC or a similar syndrome`)
            , PAIR `General Exclusion 6: wilful act or wilful negligence of the Insured`
                   (`it was` `a wilful act or wilful negligence of the Insured or a person acting for the Insured`))
    WHERE
        `it was` c MEANS elem c circumstances

-- 7(a)(i). Notwithstanding anything to the contrary, the policy does not cover loss of,
